#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&i18n-kapplication; is a chat application that lets you talk with AI "
"language models, either running locally with Ollama or provided by an online "
"AI service."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Conversations are stored in a local database on your computer, so they are "
"still there the next time you start the application. You can browse them, "
"search through them, organize them in projects and with tags, archive the "
"ones you do not need any more, and export them to a file. When you do not "
"want a conversation to be kept at all, you can use an ephemeral discussion "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&i18n-kapplication; does not provide a model of its own: it talks to a model "
"provider that you configure. Nothing is sent anywhere until you have set up "
"such a provider and asked a question."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before you can ask anything, &i18n-kapplication; needs at least one "
"<emphasis>instance</emphasis>. An instance is a configured connection to a "
"model provider: a local server running on your own machine, or an online "
"service."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first time you start the application without any instance, it offers to "
"create one. You can also open <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &i18n-kapplication;…</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> and go to the <guilabel>Instances</guilabel> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using a local model"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Running the model on your own computer keeps your questions on your machine. "
"&i18n-kapplication; can use local servers such as <application>Ollama</"
"application>, <application>llama.cpp</application> or <application>LM "
"Studio</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Install and start the server first, then add an instance of the matching "
"type. The default address of a local <application>Ollama</application> "
"server is already filled in. If <application>Ollama</application> is "
"installed but not running, &i18n-kapplication; offers to start it for you; "
"you can also do this from the command line with <userinput><command>kaichat</"
"command> <option>--start-ollama</option></userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the instance is connected you still need a model. Models can be "
"downloaded from within the instance configuration, and &i18n-kapplication; "
"notifies you when a download is finished."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using an online service"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&i18n-kapplication; can also talk to hosted services, among them Ollama "
"Cloud, OpenAI, Anthropic, Mistral AI, Groq, Grok, Qwen, OpenRouter, "
"DeepInfra, Novita AI, Cerebras and other providers with an OpenAI-compatible "
"interface. The exact list depends on the plugins installed on your system; "
"run <userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--plugin-info</option></"
"userinput> to see it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create an instance of the matching type and paste the API key given to you "
"by the service. Be aware that with an online service your questions, and any "
"file you attach, are sent to that provider and are subject to its own "
"privacy policy."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &i18n-kapplication;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "The main window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "The window is split in three parts:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the list of your chats, on the left. It can be collapsed with the button on "
"the splitter;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the conversation itself, on the right, where your questions and the answers "
"of the model are shown;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "the input field at the bottom, where you type your question."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Above them, a header bar lets you start a new chat or an ephemeral "
"discussion, mark the current chat as a favorite and search in the current "
"conversation. The status bar at the bottom shows what the model is currently "
"doing, for instance which tool it is calling."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Asking questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Type your question in the input field and validate it. The answer appears in "
"the conversation view as it is being generated, and a notification is shown "
"when a long answer is finished."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can attach files to a question, and enable the tools the model is "
"allowed to call while answering it. Each chat keeps its own history, which "
"is sent along with your new question so that the model knows the context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing chats"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Chats are created from the header bar, or with <userinput><command>kaichat</"
"command> <option>--new-chat</option> <replaceable>title</replaceable></"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right-click a chat in the list to act on it:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Modify…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change the title of the chat."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "Duplicate…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a copy of the chat, for instance to try another direction without "
"losing the original conversation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set as Favorite"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Show the chat in the <guilabel>Favorite</guilabel> section at the top of the "
"list. The same can be done with the <guibutton>Favorite</guibutton> button "
"of the header bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guisubmenu
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "Project"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Move the chat into a project, or out of it with <guimenuitem>No Project</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guisubmenu
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tags"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add tags to the chat or remove them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "Archive"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hide the chat from the list without deleting it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete the chat and its messages for good."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The other chats are grouped by age: today, the last seven days, the last "
"thirty days and older."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A conversation can also be forked from one of its messages with the "
"<guibutton>Fork</guibutton> button shown next to it. This starts a new chat "
"containing the conversation up to that message, and leaves the original chat "
"untouched."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A chat you do not need any more can be archived instead of being deleted. "
"Archived chats are hidden from the list; show them again with "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Archive</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To look for something you asked or read some time ago, use "
"<menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></"
"keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Search in Database…"
"</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. This searches the whole stored history, not "
"only the chat you are looking at. The number of matches is shown in the "
"status bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "Projects and tags"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Projects and tags are two ways of organizing your chats. A chat belongs to "
"at most one project, which is useful to keep together the conversations "
"about the same piece of work. A chat can have any number of tags."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Both are created, renamed and removed with <guimenuitem>Manage Projects…</"
"guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Manage Tags…</guimenuitem>, in the "
"<guisubmenu>Project</guisubmenu> and <guisubmenu>Tags</guisubmenu> submenus "
"of the context menu of the chat list. Removing a project does not remove its "
"chats: they are kept, outside of any project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The tag selector above the chat list only shows the chats which have one of "
"the selected tags. Select no tag to see all of them again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ephemeral discussions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An ephemeral discussion is a chat which is never written to the database. "
"Use it for a question you do not want to keep: once you close &i18n-"
"kapplication;, it is gone. Start one with the <guibutton>Ephemeral "
"Discussion</guibutton> button of the header bar, or with "
"<userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--ephemeral-chat</option> "
"<replaceable>title</replaceable></userinput>. Ephemeral discussions are "
"shown in their own section at the top of the chat list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you change your mind, the <guibutton>Save Discussion in Database</"
"guibutton> button of the header bar turns it into a normal chat."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that this only concerns what is stored on your computer: with "
"an online service, your questions are still sent to that provider."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Ask"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Quick Ask is a small dialog for a single question, without opening the main "
"window. Open it with <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open "
"Quick Ask…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, with the <keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Meta;<keycap>Space</keycap></keycombo> global shortcut, or with "
"<userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--quick-ask</option></"
"userinput>. Questions asked this way are not added to your chats, unless you "
"keep the discussion with the <guibutton>Save Discussion in Database</"
"guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid "Importing and exporting chats"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The current chat can be saved to a file with <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Export…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, in one of four "
"formats:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export as JSON…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <filename class=\"extension\">.kaichat</filename> file. This is the only "
"format that &i18n-kapplication; can read back."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export as Markdown…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "A text file keeping the formatting of the answers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export as Text…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plain text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid "Export as Pdf…"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid "A printable document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A previously exported <filename class=\"extension\">.kaichat</filename> file "
"is read back with <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Import…</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>. You can also open such a file from your file "
"manager, or pass it on the command line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adjusting the display"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The text of the whole application can be made bigger or smaller with "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Font Size</guisubmenu></"
"menuchoice>, or with <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>+</keycap></"
"keycombo> and <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>-</keycap></"
"keycombo>. A fixed font can be chosen in the configuration dialog instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>Color Scheme</"
"guisubmenu></menuchoice> switches the colors of the window without changing "
"your desktop settings, and <keycap>F11</keycap> switches to full screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The menu bar can be hidden with <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Menubar</guimenuitem></menuchoice>; the actions "
"stay available through the hamburger button of the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &i18n-kapplication;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The configuration dialog is opened with <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &i18n-kapplication;…</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>. Depending on how the application was built, it has the "
"following pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whether the system tray icon is shown, and the system prompt sent to the "
"model at the beginning of every conversation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "Font"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use a font of your choice instead of the system one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "Instances"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Add, remove and configure the connections to your model providers, and "
"manage the models available on them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "MCP Servers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Model Context Protocol servers, which give the model access to external data "
"and actions. This support is still experimental."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spell Checking"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spell checking of what you type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Text-to-speech settings, when the application was built with text-to-speech "
"support."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enable or disable the installed plugins and configure the tools the model "
"may use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Feedback"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How much information, if any, you want to send to the developers. Nothing is "
"sent unless you ask for it here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid "Retention"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How long your chats are kept. <guilabel>Retention Days</guilabel> is the "
"number of days after which old chats are removed; with the default value of "
"0, they are kept for ever. <guilabel>Exclude Favorite Chats</guilabel>, "
"enabled by default, keeps your favorite chats whatever their age."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid "Privacy"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Shows where your chats are stored on disk. The path can be copied to the "
"clipboard with the button next to it, for instance to back up or delete the "
"database."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Notifications are configured with <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Notifications…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Instances and MCP servers can also be configured outside of the application, "
"from the <guilabel>AI</guilabel> module of &systemsettings;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "Files used"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid "~/.config/kaichatrc"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid "The settings of the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid "~/.local/share/kaichat/ai-database/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The databases holding your chats and their messages. The exact location is "
"shown on the <guilabel>Privacy</guilabel> page of the configuration dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The configuration of your instances contains the API keys of the online "
"services you use. Treat these files as you would treat a password."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Line Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&i18n-kapplication; runs as a single instance: starting it again while it is "
"already running passes the options to the window that is already open "
"instead of opening a second one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "--list-instances"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid "Print the configured instances and exit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid "--list-chats"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid "Print the titles of the stored chats and exit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: index.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid "--plugin-info"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid "Print the available text and tool plugins and exit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>--instance</option> <replaceable>name</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start with a specific instance."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>--new-chat</option> <replaceable>title</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a new chat with this title."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:457
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>--ephemeral-chat</option> <replaceable>title</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a new ephemeral discussion with this title. It is not stored in the "
"database."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>--switch-to-chat</option> <replaceable>name</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:463
#, no-c-format
msgid "Switch to an existing chat, by title."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>--switch-to-chat-from-id</option> <replaceable>id</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
